msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.intro.title"
msgstr "Set up FGV OpenRank for this journal"

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.intro.description"
msgstr "The ranking block reads settings spread over several OJS screens, not only the plugin form. This guide walks through the six steps in the order they have to be done, with the path to each screen and what to check once you save."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.intro.summaryLabel"
msgstr "Guide summary"

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.intro.summary"
msgstr "Six steps: where the block goes on the homepage, which tabs it shows, the journal ISSN, the article DOIs, the \"Trending\" tab and the daily cache update."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.intro.requirements"
msgstr "Two settings live in the server’s <code>config.inc.php</code> and have no screen in the dashboard: <code>allowed_hosts</code> must include the journal’s address, otherwise every tab shows an error, and <code>api_key_secret</code> must be set before an Altmetric API key can be stored. Ask your server administrator if that is the case."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.intro.note"
msgstr "The links open the settings in another tab so this guide stays available. Nothing is saved here: close and reopen the guide whenever you like."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step1.title"
msgstr "Choose where the block goes on the homepage"

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step1.description"
msgstr "The plugin only draws the block where the position setting tells it to. With the default option it looks for the <code>&lt;div class=&quot;rankingTabs&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code> element in the journal’s \"Additional Content\" — without that element pasted there, the block shows up nowhere. The other three options, at the top, after a given section or at the bottom of the homepage, do not need \"Additional Content\"."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step1.pathPosition"
msgstr "Settings → Website → Plugins → Installed Plugins → FGV OpenRank → Settings → Position on the journal homepage → Choose the position and save."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step1.pathAdditionalContent"
msgstr "Settings → Website → Appearance → Advanced → Additional Content → Paste <code>&lt;div class=&quot;rankingTabs&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code> in each language and save."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step1.expected"
msgstr "The journal homepage starts showing the block in the chosen position, with the tabs loading the articles."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step2.title"
msgstr "Choose, order and customize the tabs"

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step2.description"
msgstr "There are five tabs: \"Most recent\", \"Most read\", \"Most cited\", \"Trending\" and \"Highlight\". The configuration grid decides which ones appear and in what order; editing a tab sets its title, description and how many articles it holds. \"Most read\" also has \"Days for most read\", the window used to count views, and \"Highlight\" has \"Custom content\", free text that replaces the article list."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step2.pathEnabled"
msgstr "Settings → Website → Plugins → Installed Plugins → FGV OpenRank → Settings → Enabled → Tick the tabs the journal will show and drag the rows to order them."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step2.pathEdit"
msgstr "Settings → Website → Plugins → Installed Plugins → FGV OpenRank → Settings → Edit → Fill in the tab title, description and number of items and save."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step2.expected"
msgstr "The block on the homepage shows only the ticked tabs, in the order you set and with the titles and descriptions you chose."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step3.title"
msgstr "Register the journal ISSN"

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step3.description"
msgstr "\"Most cited\" queries Crossref by the journal ISSN, and \"Trending\" queries Altmetric by the ISSN whenever an API key is stored. With no ISSN those two tabs have nothing to ask for and stay empty."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step3.pathIssn"
msgstr "Settings → Journal → Masthead → Online ISSN → Fill in the ISSN and save."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step3.expected"
msgstr "On the next cache update the \"Most cited\" and \"Trending\" tabs start listing articles instead of coming up empty."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step4.title"
msgstr "Assign DOIs to the articles"

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step4.description"
msgstr "\"Most cited\" and \"Trending\" identify each article by its DOI: Crossref and Altmetric return DOIs and the plugin looks up the matching article in the journal. An article with no DOI never shows up in those two tabs, however cited it is."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step4.pathEnable"
msgstr "Settings → Website → Plugins → Installed Plugins → DOI → Enabled → Tick the box."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step4.pathPrefix"
msgstr "Settings → Website → Plugins → Installed Plugins → DOI → Settings → Articles → Tick the option, fill in the DOI Prefix and save."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step4.expected"
msgstr "Every published article page starts showing its DOI, and the article becomes eligible for the \"Most cited\" and \"Trending\" tabs."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step5.title"
msgstr "Feed the \"Trending\" tab"

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step5.description"
msgstr "The \"Trending\" tab works in either of two ways. With an Altmetric API key the articles are fetched by the journal ISSN and ordered by score. With no key the tab shows the DOIs of the \"Manual DOI list\", in the order you added them, and it only accepts DOIs of articles published in this journal. While a key is stored the manual list is ignored."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step5.pathApiKey"
msgstr "Settings → Website → Plugins → Installed Plugins → FGV OpenRank → Settings → Trending → Edit → Altmetric API key → Fill in the key and save."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step5.pathDoiList"
msgstr "Settings → Website → Plugins → Installed Plugins → FGV OpenRank → Settings → Trending → Edit → Add DOI → Enter the DOI and save."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step5.expected"
msgstr "The \"Trending\" tab lists articles with the Altmetric donut beside them, ordered by score when a key is stored or in the order of the manual list when it is not."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step6.title"
msgstr "Keep the cache updated daily"

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step6.description"
msgstr "The tabs are served from a per-journal cache refreshed by the \"FGV OpenRank cache update\" scheduled task, which runs every day at midnight. Scheduled tasks are fired by the \"Acron Plugin\", or by <code>runScheduledTasks.php</code> in the server crontab. With neither of them the cache is only filled when a reader arrives and finds the tab empty, which makes that first visit slow."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step6.pathAcron"
msgstr "Settings → Website → Plugins → Installed Plugins → Acron Plugin → Enabled → Tick the box."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.step6.expected"
msgstr "The \"FGV OpenRank cache update\" task starts running on its own every day, and the tabs open with the data already in place."

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.complete.eyebrow"
msgstr "Setup complete"

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.complete.title"
msgstr "Done: check the block on the homepage"

msgid "plugins.generic.rankingPlugin.configurationGuide.complete.description"
msgstr "Open the journal homepage and click each enabled tab. If one of them shows an error message, check that the journal address is in <code>allowed_hosts</code> in <code>config.inc.php</code>. If \"Most cited\" or \"Trending\" is empty, check the ISSN and the DOIs. This guide can be reopened whenever you like, from the \"Configuration guide\" action on the plugin row."

